  <page_number>24</page_number>
  <running_head>VARIA POEMATA.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="2" para="true">NOVÆO, REDVCI.</l>
    <l n="2" para="true">QVis claustra tetri carceris abdita,</l>
    <l n="3">Quis vincla tandem rupit ahenea,</l>
    <l n="4">Plures quis amissum per annos-</l>
    <l n="5">Restituit reducem Nouæum?</l>
    <l n="6" para="true">Nam te cauernis luce carentibus-</l>
    <l n="7">Vinctum, seueris excubijs Iber-</l>
    <l n="8">Horrens tenebat, ne solutus-</l>
    <l n="9">Damna suis metuenda ferres.</l>
    <l n="10" para="true">Non tutiori carcere Virginem-</l>
    <l n="11">Seruasse prudens Acrisius pater-</l>
    <l n="12">Fertur, nec audacem catena-</l>
    <l n="13">Pirithóum grauior repressit.</l>
    <l n="14" para="true">Sed qui supremo Numine temperat-</l>
    <l n="15">Orbem, timores risit Ibericos:</l>
    <l n="16">Custode quum iussit remoto-</l>
    <l n="17">Claustra patere tibi reclufa.</l>
    <l n="18" para="true">Sic liberatum nunc precibus pi-</l>
    <l n="19">æGentis Nouæum reddit amabilem:</l>
    <l n="20">Vxoris &amp; charum redonat-</l>
    <l n="21">Fletibus egregiæ maritum:</l>
    <l n="22" para="true">Qui magna ferret commoda patriæ,</l>
    <l n="23">Qui damna pulsis adderet hostibus-</l>
    <l n="24">Dicenda, bellorum peritus-</l>
    <l n="25">Milite seu duce vellet vti</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Marginal note at bottom right, set in italic: "Qu;" (partial, as printed). Faint show-through of text from the reverse page is visible in the margins and has been omitted. Two words in the first column of the Latin ("Pirithóum" in the fourth stanza) are a probable misprint for "Pirithoum"; kept as printed with a combining accent. Greek-style heavy ornaments are decorative only.</notes>
</page>
